  "discussion": {
    "headline": "\"dog days\" of summer live up to their name through Early Next week",
    "dateLine": "11:45 a.m. Friday, August 7, 2026, Update",
    "excerpt": "Following a pleasant start to the week, southwesterly flow returned on Wednesday and ushered much hotter and steamier air back into the mid-Atlantic States. Along with the heat and humidity came showers and locally heavy, drenching thunderstorms. In fact, parts of York, Adams and Cumberland Counties received as much as 2-3\" of rain from Thursday afternoon's storms, and wind gusts reached 50-60 mph in a few spots (see below). …",
